<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs actual receipts Fri 109,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs actual receipts Fri 109,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Actual interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts on Friday were 109,000 head, versus and estimate of 105,000, USDA Market News said.</p>
<p>Actual Saturday receipts were 17,000 hogs. Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>Opening trade on Monday was not well established.  Early sales Barrows and Gilts were $.50 lower than Friday midsession. US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>			     Country		   Plants</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    55.50 -56.50	   56.50 -57.50</p>
<p>few			55.00 -57.00	   56.00 -58.00</p>
<p>Sows: 500 dn steady to 1.00 lower, 500 up steady to 2.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3</p>
<p>300-450 lbs.	   42.00 -45.00	   43.00 -47.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -46.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    47.00 -50.00	   47.00 -51.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
